Problem Title: Email Spam Filter Score Analyzer
Oliver is building an email filtering tool. Each email has a "spam score" represented as a positive integer.
Before identifying risky emails, the scores need to be modified:
If a score is greater than or equal to 50, increase it by 10.
If a score is less than 50, decrease it by 5, but not below 0.
After modifying all scores, Oliver wants to identify all scores that appear exactly once and calculate their total sum.
Constraints
If any spam score is negative in the input, display:
"Negative scores are not allowed"
All scores must be positive integers.
If no unique scores exist after modification, display:
"No unique scores found after modification"
Do not use System.exit(0).
Example Explanation
For input scores {45, 52, 45, 70, 10}:
Modify each score:
45 → 45 − 5 = 40
52 → 52 + 10 = 62
45 → 40
70 → 80
10 → 10 − 5 = 5
Modified list: {40, 62, 40, 80, 5}
Unique values: {62, 80, 5}
Sum = 62 + 80 + 5 = 147
Sample Input 1
Enter the number of emails
6
Enter the spam scores
45 52 45 70 10 85
Sample Output 1
157
Sample Input 2
Enter the number of emails
5
Enter the spam scores
55 55 60 60 70
Sample Output 2
No unique scores found after modification
Sample Input 3
Enter the number of emails
4
Enter the spam scores
20 55 -5 40
Sample Output 3
Negative scores are not allowed
